N2  - Summary Chapter 17 analyzes the integration of cybersecurity measures within the framework of space operations, addressing the growing importance of safeguarding space assets against cyber threats. The chapter begins by identifying the unique vulnerabilities of space systems, including satellites, ground stations, and communication networks. It discusses the evolving landscape of cyber threats and the necessity for robust cybersecurity strategies tailored to the complexities of space environments. Key methodologies for cybersecurity R&D are presented, emphasizing the development of innovative technologies and practices that enhance the resilience and security of space operations. The chapter also highlights the role of collaboration among government, industry, and academia in advancing research initiatives and establishing best practices. By prioritizing cybersecurity R&D in the space sector, stakeholders can ensure the integrity and availability of critical space infrastructure in an increasingly interconnected world.
